" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354908} {:answer/id #uuid "8ee2a904-7722-5877-8823-f368265253f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355924} {:answer/id #uuid "97920ae7-f871-5bcc-b433-ad7f958e4ab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355999} {:answer/id #uuid "c4d006dd-514e-5f24-b8ea-65691b567901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356383} {:answer/id #uuid "fd92fbd4-d7d1-557a-8864-0868b5fc986c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd92fbd4-d7d1-557a-8864-0868b5fc986c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356890} :answer-field/id #uuid "c702bda3-b33d-5d6a-b438-e9d3a5575649" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8b6c5226-6a4c-5905-b982-20f40f90cbd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-94093" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =2{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+(3){x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(3){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}(3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357654 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161986 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "328b0b77-f789-581e-a119-9823297666ae" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Quadratic Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "021bd2b7-706e-57b3-a8af-b3a83db7afce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354673} {:answer/id #uuid "5cd22498-12fa-59db-81fd-6c2ce36f48b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355485} {:answer/id #uuid "b63d5c18-a2a2-5302-9ff5-868dfe95946a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356266} {:answer/id #uuid "f65a1d83-e90e-527d-9df8-022f7c05907b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356809} {:answer/id #uuid "fd26311c-2f18-574d-9496-266fed0c1d74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b63d5c18-a2a2-5302-9ff5-868dfe95946a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356266} :answer-field/id #uuid "09e70103-bd6b-5347-8799-710e68326fdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96f2319e-e633-542e-b1fa-62302f0afd32" :question/math-academy-id "q-94099" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =2{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+1{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+(-2){x}_{2}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})+{x}_{3}(2{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{x}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357656 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161986 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "328b0b77-f789-581e-a119-9823297666ae" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Quadratic Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "074bc0a8-4ace-5935-8132-e8516c14bc11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354727} {:answer/id #uuid "0c35860c-44ad-5b5c-89ff-8920a976c568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354776} {:answer/id #uuid "29a555f5-45bd-56ad-b133-4ea913d8ef19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355011} {:answer/id #uuid "6211823f-d038-5a7f-841f-e14f57f1ed54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-3{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355538} {:answer/id #uuid "aa727819-380a-594d-a4bd-a5f02c1e6dbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "074bc0a8-4ace-5935-8132-e8516c14bc11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354727} :answer-field/id #uuid "135db05c-789b-5517-a595-77d2c4b006a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fee716f7-a185-58ac-8ee8-36859424ee03" :question/math-academy-id "q-94105" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{2}+(-1){x}_{2}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+(-1){x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({x}_{1})+{x}_{2}(2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3})+{x}_{3}(-{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357660 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161987 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb93c0ea-26d9-5190-9677-b8c7eb6f7ef1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Quadratic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02a9e9a8-3c46-5c6f-a0b9-c715263b46fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354679} {:answer/id #uuid "70d8b306-7d64-5a53-bf09-1fcafe21fe9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355662} {:answer/id #uuid "cacc7a23-abd5-5d11-b9dd-14002a05348f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356433} {:answer/id #uuid "cc6a54ea-970f-5bca-8ce6-3a18756c0f41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356448} {:answer/id #uuid "d57fe9de-2cd2-5256-980e-2266baf495ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cacc7a23-abd5-5d11-b9dd-14002a05348f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356433} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a785e93-2dfe-5d3a-8afd-c6a0e1ac5840" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357165}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6a58c19a-d8e2-5b8b-a8c1-6d0a7f511f7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-94115" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & b \\\\ b & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ is given above. What is the value of $b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+1{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,1{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+(-2){x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must split the coefficient of $2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries \n\n$$\n{a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{2}{2}=1\n$$\n\nof our matrix. So, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $b=1$ and $c=-2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\nb+c=1-2=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357663 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161987 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb93c0ea-26d9-5190-9677-b8c7eb6f7ef1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Quadratic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26e98748-b388-5506-aac1-9e30f72043d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354991} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd9af0b-3c0e-55a4-a669-bcadc34c08b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355216} {:answer/id #uuid "4978df42-b859-52a6-ba63-1a347384a158" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355314} {:answer/id #uuid "e34d7105-1d3f-5ec1-968a-d5410c870152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356653} {:answer/id #uuid "e64af5fe-d6ac-5ec1-be75-b923dae80e06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e34d7105-1d3f-5ec1-968a-d5410c870152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356653} :answer-field/id #uuid "57a91600-a00a-59db-b63e-edcd7437f52e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b751a90c-cbe5-589a-aef5-36f0a41388ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-94120" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & b \\\\ 6 & a & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+12{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+12{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-2){x}_{1}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,6{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{2}^{2}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,(-2){x}_{3}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must do the following splits:\n\n- we split the coefficient of $12{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries ${a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{12}{2}=6,$ and\n\n- we split the coefficient of $-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}$ between the entries ${a}_{13}={a}_{31}=\\frac{-4}{2}=-2.$\n\nSo, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=0.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+(-2)+0=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186491163 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161987 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb93c0ea-26d9-5190-9677-b8c7eb6f7ef1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Quadratic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c4b303a-da20-585c-9039-a200f7b368d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490659} {:answer/id #uuid "87a1133a-4a67-519e-80d8-5e89f39e7463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490782} {:answer/id #uuid "8d4ddb5f-1beb-5278-b235-e2351d1aa9fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490793} {:answer/id #uuid "96b12f22-924f-5fb6-9f0b-8395ca5aa73b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490818} {:answer/id #uuid "eaafedd0-2b42-5f65-9544-d14ab90678c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d4ddb5f-1beb-5278-b235-e2351d1aa9fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490793} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a88c7b8-264d-5d69-ba62-b1d185359ee8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491005}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "73743ec2-4a1f-56a6-9413-8c931a00dbaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-94121" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & b & c \\\\ 1 & c & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+4{x}_{2}^{2}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-2{x}_{3}^{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+4{x}_{2}^{2}-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+1{x}_{1}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,0{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}^{2}+(-4){x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,1{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+(-4){x}_{3}{x}_{2}+(-2){x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must do the following splits:\n\n- we split the coefficient of $2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}$ between the entries ${a}_{13}={a}_{31}=\\frac{2}{2}=1,$ and\n\n- we split the coefficient of $-8{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ between the entries ${a}_{23}={a}_{32}=\\frac{-8}{2}=-4.$\n\nSo, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3,$ $b=4,$ and $c=-4.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=3+4+(-4)=3.\n$$"}]}
